  "prefLabel": "Frl 601.01 Definitions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Frl 601.01 Definitions.\n\n(a) “Funeral chapel” means a location at which funeral services are provided, but which does not have a preparation room.\n\n(b) “Funeral home” means “funeral home” as defined in RSA 325:1, IX, namely, “every place or premise devoted to or used in the care and preparation for the funeral and burial of dead human bodies or maintained for the convenience of the bereaved for viewing or other services in connection with dead human bodies or as an office or place for carrying on the profession of funeral directing.”\n\nSource. #1689, eff 12-22-80; ss by#2344, eff 4-15-83; ss by #2986, eff 3-18-85; ss by #4357, eff 1-20-88, EXPIRED: 1-20-94\n\nNew. #10988, eff 12-7-15; ss by #14646, eff 9-4-26, EXPIRES: 9-4-36",
